.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-HEADLAMP-INSTALL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-headlamp-install
.Nd fetch the Headlamp Kubernetes interface for the web console \(em which upstream no longer publishes
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa kldload-headlamp.service
runs
.Nm
before starting Headlamp behind the web console's
.Pa /k8s/
path.
It does nothing when the pinned version is already installed, installs
from
.Pa /var/lib/kldload/headlamp-cache/
when a copy is there, and otherwise downloads the server from Headlamp's
GitHub releases.
.Pp
Headlamp stopped publishing a standalone server; the download fails, and
the build leaves
.Pa kldload-headlamp.service
disabled so that no install carries a failing unit.
The web console's Kubernetes terminal,
.Pa /k9s/ ,
is unaffected.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev HEADLAMP_VER
The version; default 0.26.0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/headlamp/headlamp-server
The installed server.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/headlamp-cache/headlamp-server- Ns Ar version
A copy to install from instead of the network.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when installed; 1 when it could not be.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-webui 8 ,
.Xr kube-cluster 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-05-17 the download was found to return 404; the service has been
disabled at build since.
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: its message still said to retry once
the network was up.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It needs rewriting \(em the server is inside the desktop application's
archive, or Headlamp can be deployed into the cluster with its Helm
chart \(em before the service is worth enabling.
Nothing it downloads is checked against a published sum.
